  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4103.15 Flying bug insecticide",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4103.15 “Flying bug insecticide” means any insecticide product that is designed for use against flying insects or other flying arthropods, including but not limited to flies, mosquitoes, moths, or gnats. The term does not include wasp and hornet insecticides, products that are designed to be used exclusively on humans or animals or their bedding, or any moth-proofing product.\n\nSource. #10527, eff 2-26-14; ss by #13969, eff 5-21-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4100.html"
